<h1>vexes Wiki</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Documentation for an experimental dependency-evidence CLI. This copy follows the v{{ versions.vexes.sourceVersion }} source tree; npm <code>latest</code> is currently v{{ versions.vexes.version }}.</p>

<div class="warning-box"><strong>Do not read a quiet result as “safe.”</strong> vexes can match supported dependency coordinates to OSV and surface bounded heuristic evidence. It can miss malicious behavior, report benign behavior, or return incomplete evidence. Incomplete requested checks exit 2.</div>

<h2>Current scope</h2>
<ul>
  <li>OSV advisory matching across {{ versions.vexes.ecosystems }} ecosystems and {{ versions.vexes.inputs }} recognized dependency input forms.</li>
  <li>Heuristic registry and bounded selected-file analysis for npm and PyPI only.</li>
  <li>JSON and SARIF output for automation, with some early/setup/watch paths still outside the uniform schema.</li>
  <li>An explicit, experimental, public-registry npm guard. There are no automatic shell wrappers in the current release.</li>
  <li>Zero external runtime npm dependencies. Vendored code, Node.js, upstream APIs, and the scanner implementation remain part of the trust surface.</li>
</ul>

